Images
description: the common rasters and SVG shown directly; TIFF, PSD, HEIC decoded first
- >
  `png`, `jpeg`, `gif`, `webp`, `avif`, `bmp`, `ico`, and `svg` display directly, with
  thumbnails in the tree views. Region FRAGMENTS and annotations attach to an image, so a
  marked-up photo is an addressable, taggable node.
- >
  Formats browsers refuse are decoded client-side first: `tiff`, `psd` (Photoshop, flattened),
  `heic`.
- >
  In a chapter, an image member (`- *: photo.png`) IS the figure - embedding is structural
  (docs/documents/marklower/embeds), never a text token.
